# 4. Input / Output & Type Casting

```python
name = input("Naam batao: ")     # hamesha string return karta hai
age = int(input("Age: "))
print("Hello", name, "age", age)
print("A", "B", sep="-", end="!\n")   # A-B!
```

**f-string (best way):**
```python
name, pi = "Amit", 3.14159
print(f"Name: {name}, Pi: {pi:.2f}")     # 2 decimal
print(f"{1000000:,}")                    # 1,000,000
print(f"{name!r}")                       # repr
print(f"{5:05d}")                        # 00005
print(f"{name:>10}|{name:<10}|{name:^10}")  # align
print(f"{x=}") if (x:=5) else None       # x=5 (debug, 3.8+)
```

**Type Casting:**
```python
int("10"), float("3.5"), str(10), bool(0), list("abc"), tuple([1,2]), set([1,1,2])
```
**Falsy values:** `0, 0.0, "", [], (), {}, set(), None, False`. Baaki sab Truthy.

