# 8. Set

**Kya hai?** Unordered, unique elements, mutable collection (hash-based).
**Kyun?** Duplicates hatane, fast membership check O(1), math set operations.
**Kab?** Unique items chahiye, common/different items find karne ho.

```python
s = {1, 2, 3, 3}     # {1,2,3}
empty = set()        # {} dict banata hai!
```

## 🔥 Set Methods

| Method | Kaam |
|--------|------|
| `add(x)` | Ek element add |
| `update(iter)` | Multiple add |
| `remove(x)` | Hatao (nahi mila → KeyError) |
| `discard(x)` | Hatao (nahi mila → no error) |
| `pop()` | Random element hatao |
| `clear()` | Sab hatao |
| `copy()` | Copy |
| `union(b)` / `a \| b` | Dono ke sab |
| `intersection(b)` / `a & b` | Common |
| `difference(b)` / `a - b` | a me jo b me nahi |
| `symmetric_difference(b)` / `a ^ b` | Jo common nahi |
| `issubset(b)` / `a <= b` | a, b ka subset? |
| `issuperset(b)` / `a >= b` | a, b ka superset? |
| `isdisjoint(b)` | Koi common nahi? |
| `intersection_update`, `difference_update`, `symmetric_difference_update` | In-place versions |

```python
a = {1,2,3}; b = {3,4,5}
print(a | b)   # {1,2,3,4,5}
print(a & b)   # {3}
print(a - b)   # {1,2}
print(a ^ b)   # {1,2,4,5}
```

**Real Example — Duplicate hatao (order maintain):**
```python
nums = [1,2,2,3,1]
print(list(set(nums)))          # order guaranteed nahi
print(list(dict.fromkeys(nums)))  # order maintain ✅
```

